WEBVTT

00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:02.047 --> 00:00:06.821
In the earlier lessons, we learned classic, volume and hybrid lashes,

00:00:06.771 --> 00:00:08.669
and how to draw a lash map.

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:12.910
Today we take a step back, to the first ten minutes of the appointment.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.150
Nobody takes photos of these ten minutes, and nobody praises them.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:21.983
But they decide whether the set will last, and, even more important,

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:23.710
whether the client is safe.

00:00:24.347 --> 00:00:26.047
Here is something that happens a lot.

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:30.092
The salon is busy, the technician is in a hurry, says hello,

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:32.607
and has the client lie down straight away.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.567
No questions, no close look at the eyes.

00:00:36.148 --> 00:00:38.687
A few days later, the client sends a message:

00:00:38.958 --> 00:00:41.887
her eyelids are swollen, itchy and red.

00:00:42.392 --> 00:00:43.922
Only then, when you ask,

00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:47.807
do you find out she once reacted to lash glue at another salon.

00:00:48.058 --> 00:00:50.527
One question at the start would have prevented it.

00:00:50.841 --> 00:00:55.487
That is why every appointment starts with a consultation, even with regular clients.

00:00:56.024 --> 00:00:57.020
So what do you ask?

00:00:57.344 --> 00:00:58.460
Allergies first.

00:00:58.805 --> 00:01:02.837
Has the client ever reacted to lash glue, to lash or brow tint,

00:01:02.787 --> 00:01:04.860
or to cosmetics around the eyes?

00:01:05.212 --> 00:01:06.620
Then ask about the eyes:

00:01:06.969 --> 00:01:11.340
does she often have dry eyes, red eyes, or an inflamed lash line?

00:01:11.753 --> 00:01:14.940
Has she recently had eye surgery, or any treatment on her eyes?

00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:17.340
Does the client wear contact lenses?

00:01:17.518 --> 00:01:18.860
Is she taking any medication?

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:24.380
Some medicines, such as certain allergy or acne medicines, can dry the eyes.

00:01:24.728 --> 00:01:28.318
And if the client is pregnant, that is a reason to ask more carefully,

00:01:28.268 --> 00:01:32.060
and to follow the glue maker's instructions and the advice where you work.

00:01:32.476 --> 00:01:35.020
We are lash technicians, not doctors.

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:37.260
Never give medical advice yourself.

00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:40.874
Only after the safety questions do we ask about the look.

00:01:41.203 --> 00:01:44.394
Does the client want natural lashes, or something fuller?

00:01:44.811 --> 00:01:46.074
What does she do for work?

00:01:46.355 --> 00:01:50.350
Does she often swim or use the sauna, does she rub her eyes,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.994
does she sleep face down?

00:01:52.582 --> 00:01:55.994
And be honest with her about how much her natural lashes can carry.

00:01:56.502 --> 00:02:00.554
For choosing a style to suit the eye shape, go back to the lash mapping lesson.

00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:03.515
Then look at the client's eyes, in good light.

00:02:03.993 --> 00:02:10.075
Red or watery eyes, a stye, a swollen or crusty lash line, or recent eye surgery:

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.115
then not today.

00:02:11.616 --> 00:02:14.004
The full list, and how to say no kindly,

00:02:13.954 --> 00:02:16.635
is in the lesson on when not to do a service.

00:02:17.273 --> 00:02:18.912
Now let's talk about the glue,

00:02:18.862 --> 00:02:21.772
because the glue is the main reason for all this care.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:26.652
Lash glue is cyanoacrylate, and it cures with the moisture in the air.

00:02:27.071 --> 00:02:29.452
While it cures, it gives off fumes.

00:02:29.713 --> 00:02:31.197
The fumes sting the eyes,

00:02:31.147 --> 00:02:35.212
so the client's eyes must stay fully closed for the whole appointment.

00:02:35.706 --> 00:02:36.972
And the most important point:

00:02:37.338 --> 00:02:39.852
an allergy to the glue can build up gradually.

00:02:40.027 --> 00:02:43.932
Some clients have ten sets with no problem, and react on the eleventh.

00:02:44.102 --> 00:02:47.452
The same goes for technicians, who breathe the fumes every day.

00:02:47.638 --> 00:02:50.972
You'll find this in detail in the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:02:51.507 --> 00:02:53.305
That is why there is a patch test.

00:02:53.556 --> 00:02:58.055
Many glue makers and many salons advise a test before the first set,

00:02:58.005 --> 00:03:01.065
usually 24 to 48 hours before the appointment.

00:03:01.388 --> 00:03:03.465
Do the test the way the glue maker says.

00:03:03.817 --> 00:03:06.868
Usually you attach a few lashes at the outer corner,

00:03:06.818 --> 00:03:09.465
or put a tiny dot of glue near the lash line,

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:10.905
and send the client home.

00:03:11.171 --> 00:03:15.625
The client watches for redness, itching or swelling, and lets the salon know.

00:03:16.212 --> 00:03:17.702
But understand this correctly:

00:03:17.955 --> 00:03:20.022
a patch test is not a guarantee.

00:03:20.518 --> 00:03:24.502
No reaction to the test does not mean there will never be a reaction later.

00:03:24.845 --> 00:03:27.622
It only helps you spot the clients who are already sensitive.

00:03:27.971 --> 00:03:30.742
So every time the client comes back, still ask:

00:03:31.091 --> 00:03:34.022
after your last appointment, did you have any trouble with your eyes?

00:03:34.449 --> 00:03:38.422
If she says yes, stop, and do not go ahead until it is clear.

00:03:39.092 --> 00:03:43.321
And if the client reports redness, itching or swelling after the test,

00:03:43.271 --> 00:03:44.753
then no lashes that day.

00:03:45.226 --> 00:03:48.433
Tell her very gently, and advise her to ask a doctor.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.002
Some technicians hate to lose the client,

00:03:50.952 --> 00:03:53.713
so they switch to a different glue and go ahead anyway.

00:03:54.123 --> 00:03:55.153
Never do that.

00:03:55.495 --> 00:03:58.331
You don't know which ingredient the client reacts to,

00:03:58.281 --> 00:04:00.433
and next time the reaction may be worse.

00:04:00.693 --> 00:04:04.753
Write down the result, so nobody at the salon does the service by mistake.

00:04:05.385 --> 00:04:07.490
The room is part of the preparation too.

00:04:07.881 --> 00:04:10.965
Each glue maker gives a humidity and temperature range,

00:04:10.915 --> 00:04:13.170
and you keep the room within that range,

00:04:13.279 --> 00:04:14.770
as we said in the classic lesson.

00:04:15.109 --> 00:04:18.626
Keep the room well ventilated, close the glue bottle straight away,

00:04:18.576 --> 00:04:21.730
and never place the glue drop right under the client's nose.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.490
Then hygiene.

00:04:23.892 --> 00:04:25.143
The bed is wiped down,

00:04:25.093 --> 00:04:28.530
and the cover and headrest liner are changed for every client.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:33.170
Lash wands, micro brushes and under eye pads are single use.

00:04:33.599 --> 00:04:36.732
Tweezers are cleaned and disinfected after every client,

00:04:36.682 --> 00:04:39.650
as in the lesson on handling tools after each client.

00:04:40.149 --> 00:04:42.930
The client lies close to your face for two hours.

00:04:43.119 --> 00:04:45.730
A clean workspace puts her at ease at first sight.

00:04:46.396 --> 00:04:47.982
Finally, keep a record.

00:04:48.243 --> 00:04:52.981
The client's answers, the date of the patch test, the result, the glue used,

00:04:52.931 --> 00:04:54.461
the length and the curl.

00:04:54.952 --> 00:04:59.102
Many salons also have the client read and agree in writing before the first set.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:03.947
In VaraaAi, you write this in the internal notes in the client's profile,

00:05:03.897 --> 00:05:05.662
which only the salon can see.

00:05:06.006 --> 00:05:08.371
This is health information, and private,

00:05:08.321 --> 00:05:12.942
so only record it with the client's consent, and keep it strictly confidential.

00:05:13.284 --> 00:05:17.582
Next time, whoever does the lashes, opening the profile tells them everything.

00:05:18.242 --> 00:05:19.031
So you see.

00:05:19.272 --> 00:05:21.191
The first ten minutes are not difficult.

00:05:21.222 --> 00:05:22.231
Just don't skip them:

00:05:22.506 --> 00:05:26.151
ask, look, test, clean, and record.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.866
Do all these small things, and when you pick up your tweezers,

00:05:29.816 --> 00:05:31.431
you can be completely at ease.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:35.111
In the practice lesson, we'll go through it step by step together.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.911
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:38.252 --> 00:05:38.951
See you next time.
